{"classified_as":[{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300046300","label":"photographs","type":"Type"},{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/archive/component/aspace_c146c16ade7c5c661c317154ee07ed43","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"aspace_c146c16ade7c5c661c317154ee07ed43","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"accession number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355"}],"content":"2006.6.222","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Mym Tuma and her works","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Unknown","id":"actor/ulan/500125274","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Related Material","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/relatedmaterial"}],"content":[],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Restrictions on use","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/userestrict"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003ewww.okeeffemuseum.org/image-rights-and-reproductions/\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Legal status statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/userestrict"}],"content":null,"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"abstract","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/abstract"}],"content":"Photograph of Mym Tuma with her works. Mym Tuma, also known as Marilynn Thuma, corresponded with Georgia O'Keeffe from 1964 to 1973. This photograph, and fourteen others, were probably enclosed in a letter from Marilynn Thuma dated September 4, 1970. Handwritten on verso: \"These Forms are: Mariposa (Butterfly) 35' x 45'  Almeja (clam) 28' x 36' Cuerno (horn) Only a part of Alcatraz the white lily can be seen on the table 48' x 3